msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today, we release Quarkus 2.3.0.Final which includes a lot of refinements "
"and improvements and some new features:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev Service for Neo4J"
msgstr ""

msgid "Logging with Panache"
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing support for CLI applications"
msgstr ""

msgid "MongoDB Liquibase extension"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for Hibernate ORM interceptors"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 2.2, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-2.3[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev Services start the required containers automatically when you are "
"developing or testing your application."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A lot of Quarkus extensions are already covered and, in 2.3, we added link:/"
"guides/neo4j[a Dev Service for Neo4J]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Logging in Quarkus now has a Panache flavor which allows you to eliminate "
"logger related boilerplate code. See the link:/guides/logging[logging guide] "
"for details."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus now provides `@QuarkusMainTest` and `@QuarkusMainIntegrationTest` to "
"facilitate testing of CLI applications. Check out the link:/guides/command-"
"mode-reference[command mode guide] for details."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The new `quarkus-liquibase-mongodb` introduces support for Liquibase "
"migrations to Quarkus applications that use MongoDB."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for Hibernate Interceptors"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"link:https://docs.jboss.org/hibernate/orm/5.6/userguide/html_single/"
"Hibernate_User_Guide.html#events[Hibernate Interceptors] are now supported "
"in Quarkus. The link:/guides/hibernate-orm[Hibernate guide] provides all the "
"necessary details."
msgstr ""

